{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1521189-w20-mini-splat-witches-and-witchers","id":1521189,"title":"(W20) Mini Splat: Witches and Witchers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-22T08:47:06-07:00","id":1521189,"title":"(W20) Mini Splat: Witches and Witchers","content":"<b>What is this?</b> An alternative take on shamans and wise folk who use their relationship with the spirit world to harness power.<br /> <br /> <b>Why is this?</b> It started as a quick way to create NPCs outside the Fera with strong ties to the spirit world, but within the Revised/W20 rule-set. I wanted something for shamans that sets them apart from Sorcerers and Mages, and closer to the framework of Spirits as portrayed in WtA. Something that would still work for a paleolithic shaman, without the formalized trappings of Mage and Sorcerer.<br /> <br /> <b>Who are they? </b>Mortals who have been touched by spirits in some way. Maybe a Spirit took a fancy on them, or they have been introduced by a Mentor, or there is an actual Spirit in their ancestral line. They could be Kinfolk, or distant relation remnants of the lost breeds. Or they could have simply fallen into the role by circumstance.<br /> <br /> <b>Why witches?</b> Because their connection to the Spirit world and how the mechanics play out are very close to folklore around wise folk. Plus the term is not as occupied by canon material as \u2018shaman\u2019 is.<br /> <br /> <b>What are they (not)?</b> They are not Sorcerers, Psychics, Shapechangers or Mages. They do not possess any inherent powers, instead they rely entirely on the powers granted by Spirits. They are Spirit Mediums, perhaps somewhat similar to Enchanted from CtD.<br /> <br /> <b>But why a PC splat?</b> I want to be able to offer it as an option for a potential new player. Also, why not?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Key Traits</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Spiritual Awareness</b><br /> All witches possess a degree of Spiritual Awareness. This is covered by a Perception + Awareness roll against the local Gauntlet strength. A single success is enough to sense the presence of a Spirit, while additional successes allow to see, hear, and converse with it.<br /> <br /> <b>Numina</b><br /> A Numen (pl. Numina) in this case is a Spirit Familiar, not to be confused with the inherent powers of psychics and sorcerers. Maybe the overlapping terminology hints at the origins of the latter. For witches, this means a close Spirit ally they know and have worked with for a long time. They have at least a cordial relationship, but more often the social bond is closer to a friendship, as far as the strange mindset of Spirits allows. Witches can have several Numina.<br /> <br /> <b>Totem</b><br /> Most witches will have a personal Totem. They are very likely the ones who introduced the character to the Spirit world in the first place. Some witches will petition a Totem on their own instead, but getting their interest is not an easy task in either case. This should be something covered by the character\u2019s background.<br /> <br /> To use Pack Totems from Werewolf, divide their cost by two (rounded up) and ignore their Pack benefits. Otherwise you can follow the rules given in W20 for personal Totems. For the replacement of mechanics that are only applicable to Fera, see below.<br /> <br /> <b>Chiminage</b><br /> Chiminage is a trackable stat for witches. It represents the goodwill of each Numen towards the character, and is used in exchange for providing their Charms and powering Gifts. The type of Chiminage a Numen prefers corresponds with a type of Renown.<br /> <br /> <b>Charms</b><br /> Charms are the native powers of Spirits. A Numen can use these on behalf of the witch in exchange for Chiminage.<br /> <br /> <b>Gifts</b><br /> Witches can learn Gifts from Spirits just like Fera, although this is limited to Gifts that do not require the anatomy of a Shapechanger. Because they do not have Rage or Gnosis, they rely on their Numina to provide those for them should the Gift require it. In exchange for Chiminage, of course.<br /> <br /> <b>Rites</b><br /> A witch can learn any Rite that does not require specific Fera anatomy. Finding a teacher is probably the hardest part, although some Spirits teach Rites and a few are recorded in folk traditions.<br /> <br /> <b>General Replacements</b><br /> Use the following replacements when rules call for them:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"271\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Rage Point, Gnosis Point</td> <td width=\"354\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Chiminage</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"271\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Permanent Rage, Permanent Gnosis</td> <td width=\"354\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Sum of the two highest Numen Ranks.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"271\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Renown, Rank*</td> <td width=\"354\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Highest Numen Rank of a compatible Type</td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">*Renown and Rank replacements only apply when they are called for in general mechanics, never for social interactions with Fera.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Character Creation</b></span><br /> <br /> Mostly standard: Attributes (6/4/3), Abilities (11/7/4), Backgrounds 5, Willpower 5. You have 21 Freebie points.<br /> <br /> Characters additionally get 5 points of Numen Ranks (none higher than 3 at this point).<br /> <br /> To create a Numen, choose what kind of Spirit they are and the Type that matches it. Type is a combination of Triatic aspect and Renown, for example \u201cWeaver / Wisdom\u201d or \u201cWyrm / Cunning\u201d. You can use the Renown block on a Werewolf character sheet to write those in, together with their Rank and starting Chiminage (Rank x2). A Numen Rank caps at 5.<br /> <br /> For each point of Numen Rank, choose a Charm the Numen has (so a total of 5 at this point). You can note those in the Gifts blocks. Also, choose three Level 1 Gifts that are taught by Spirits who fit the Types of your Numina.<br /> <br /> <b>Freebie Points</b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"120\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><b>Trait</b></td> <td width=\"62\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><b>Cost</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"120\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Attribute</td> <td width=\"62\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">5 per dot</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"120\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Ability</td> <td width=\"62\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">2 per dot</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"120\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Numen Rank</td> <td width=\"62\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">7 per dot</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_t