h=\"62\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"120\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Numen Rank</td> <td width=\"62\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">CR x7</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"120\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">New Numen</td> <td width=\"62\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">7</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"120\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Background</td> <td width=\"62\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">CR x3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"120\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Willpower</td> <td width=\"62\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">CR</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"120\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Gift</td> <td width=\"62\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Level x5</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"120\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">New Rite</td> <td width=\"62\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\">Level</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <b>Using Numina and Chiminage</b><br /> To access the Charms of your Numina, you ask them nicely, and spend a point of Chiminage. You also do this if they need to jump in and provide Rage or Gnosis for your Gifts \u2013 each point of those translates to a point of Chiminage as well. If a Numen is in a bad mood or disposition towards the character, that price can go up. On the flip-side, if you encounter something that particularly entices action from a Numen, they could just as easily use a Charm of their own volition without asking for anything in return. Numina are <i>not bound</i>, but follow the character around because of mutual trust and quid pro quo. They are, like all free spirits, their own personality and should be treated as such.<br /> <br /> <b>Regaining Chiminage Points</b><br /> Chiminage works just as it does for Fera, the only difference is you pay in advance and gain boons to call in later, represented by the Chiminage pools. Additionally, if the character performs an action that would usually earn them Renown, they can translate this into Chiminage for Numina of the appropriate type.<br /> <br /> <br /> Feedback, criticism, and ideas are very welcome. Also let me know if this would be something you would be interested in playing or not, or whether you would prefer a shaman character with RAW rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T11:48:17-07:00","id":1521209,"title":"","content":"I... could say a lot but I'm not sure it'd go well. You ask why not? There's a hell of a lot of &quot;definitely not&quot; in this.<br /> <br /> I don't see a single point to using this over the existing Backgrounds, Merits, and Numina in the books for making mortal shamans and other practitioners of animistic magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T12:20:06-07:00","id":1521212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1521189-w20-mini-splat-witches-and-witchers?p=1521209#post1521209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I... could say a lot but I'm not sure it'd go well. You ask why not? There's a hell of a lot of &quot;definitely not&quot; in this.<br /> <br /> I don't see a single point to using this over the existing Backgrounds, Merits, and Numina in the books for making mortal shamans and other practitioners of animistic magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't hold back, I asked for criticism. If it's a bad idea, it's a bad idea - if I didn't anticipate that kind of feedback, I wouldn't have posted it.<br /> <br /> I can at least give some of the reasons I would prefer it, which are of course personal:<br /> <br /> - I <i>really </i>do not like that existing Numina (the power kind) which deal with Spirits are a power stat of the character and use the same mechanics like throwing fireballs. The powers of a shaman should come from the Spirits, not the shaman.<br /> <br /> - Existing Backgrounds, Merits, and Numina that access a Spirit's power are extremely vague towards the extent these powers can have. Charms and Gifts are well defined.<br /> <br /> - Everything you need to run this is in the Core rules. It plugs into the system instead putting additional mechanics on top of it. I will be honest, trying to make a working shaman with the Kinfolk rules is a pain, and using Sorcerer rules can be awkward because it's not geared towards WtA.<br /> <br /> Edit: I still appreciate the honesty- just because I think those points are good doesn't make it an attractive to others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 08-22-2023, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T22:42:32-07:00","id":1521233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1521189-w20-mini-splat-witches-and-witchers#post1521189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Why is this?</b> It started as a quick way to create NPCs outside the Fera with strong ties to the spirit world, but within the Revised/W20 rule-set. I wanted something for shamans that sets them apart from Sorcerers and Mages, and closer to the framework of Spirits as portrayed in WtA. Something that would still work for a paleolithic shaman, without the formalized trappings of Mage and Sorcerer..</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you can get everything you'd want by using the Sorcerer rules (and their various spin offs), but restricting what kind of Paths and Merits and Backgrounds work best.<br /> <br /> Keep Paths restricted to appropriate flavor like Ephemera, Divination, and Herbalism. Have Merits like Special Friend, Spirit Guide and Totem. Backgrounds like Familiar and Mentor.<br /> <br /> You can create very strong, targeted mortals with supernatural abilities with whatever flavor text you like by using Sorcerer. The issue is keeping things targeted as opposed to letting players buy whatever the hell they like because they have build points or XP and never mind if their concept and improvements makes sense with their concept.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T06:15:46-07:00","id":1521252,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1521189-w20-mini-splat-witches-and-witchers?p=1521233#post1521233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you can get everything you'd want by using the Sorcerer rules (and their various spin offs), but restricting what kind of Paths and Merits and Backgrounds work best.<br /> <br /> Keep Paths restricted to appropriate flavor like Ephemera, Divination, and Herbalism. Have Merits like Special Friend, Spirit Guide and Totem. Backgrounds like Familiar and Mentor.<br /> <br /> You can create very strong, targeted mortals with supernatural abilities with whatever flavor text you like by using Sorcerer. The issue is keeping things targeted as opposed to letting players buy whatever the hell they like because they have build points or XP and never mind if their concept and improvements makes sense with their concept.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That's how I did it in the past, but.. it's a process. You have to be willing to mix and match various books to get something that is workable.<br /> <br /> Let me make an example:<br /> I will go through a quick character creation process using Sorcerer 20 as a base. My concept for the shaman is an urban eco-terrorist who targets corporate destruction of nature, or \u2018if Poison Ivy was a shaman\u2019 so we know what we\u2019re looking at. I will skip Attributes, Abilities, and other trivial stuff for brevity.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My targets for the build are:<br /> - has a Totem and can talk to it<br /> - can talk to and call on Spirits<br /> - has a Spirit companion<br /> - can use plants offensively<br /> - can mix poisons<br /> - maybe has a few Rites</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I think that's a sensible list.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Let's start with the Totem. <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Fireweed_(Totem)\" target=\"_blank\">Fireweed</a> seem</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">s</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> a good choice:<br /> Sorcerer 20 uses the Mage 20 Totem Background. To get a Totem that is workable within the WtA context (infrequent interactions, it can talk to me, maybe helps in a pinch) we want it at Rank 3. M20 charges double for Tote</span>m, so we'll need to invest our 5 Background points and one freebie into it. We don't even get the listed benefits of the Totem, because M20 overrides it with fixed Ability bonuses.<br /> <br /> This is a personal opinion, but I don't think a shaman player should need to dump their complete starting Background points into a trait that is pretty essential to the concept, and Fireweed isn't even one of the big guns. So I can offer using the W20 Totem Background, which cuts the cost in half. Or if I feel super generous, the Sorcerer 1e Totem Merit which just lets you pick any Totem, plus it can teach you Gifts. As a side note, Kinfolk 20 outright bans the Totem Background.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Next, interaction with Spirits:<br /> Ephemera 2 to call on a type of spirit (Plant). If I want to call on a specific Spirit, Ephemera 3. Sorcerer 20 completely skips over the communication part of the Path, but we will assume it also includes being able to actually talk to Spirits.<br /> It's worth noting that the Path got a lot harder to use since Sorcerer 1e. Calling a Plant Jaggling in S20 RAW would cost 1 WP and requires 5 successes of an Attribute + Ability roll against 6. In Sorcerer 1e the interaction is free and only needs a single success. I like Ephemera, I really do. But seeing a player spend WP and fail their roll just trying to reach out to a Spirit felt so bad I house-ruled it away. For a new player I would probably recommend the classic version and treat it as a general Numen, not Sorcery specifically.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Spirit companion:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The M20/S20 Familiar Background really isn\u2019t usable in a WtA context, since Familiars in Mage deal with Quintessence and Paradox. We will substitute this with the Numen Background from <i>Player\u2019s Guide to the Garou</i>. Our Character doesn\u2019t have Gnosis to offer their companion, so we will change that to Chiminage (see what I did there?).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Fun with plants:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Nope. S20 doesn\u2019t offer anything in this regard, and I included this just to point out that Sorcerer does not offer a good spread of shaman adjacent powers. To further complicate the issue, if I wanted to pick Animal Psychics I would have to jump through the hoops of combining Sorcery and Psychic Phenomena, which is heavily discouraged. There\u2019s Spirit Chasing from Kinfolk 20, but the author halfway forgot the Path isn\u2019t exclusive to animal Spirits. If I would allow Gifts to this effect, there is a whole package of things to do to make Gifts actually work for Sorcerers.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">For completeness sake let\u2019s just say I would import Green Path from V20.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Poisons:<br /> Herbalism is an easy choice. Done.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Rites:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The default for a Sorcerer are Rituals. RAW we would get a few of them in chargen, and I would give the option to substitute them with Rites. This isn\u2019t explicitly covered by the rules, but imo it should be for shaman characters.</span></span><br /> <br /> ---------<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">So, after all that, can I create a working mortal shaman character for WtA with the current rules under S20? Yes, if I use a dozen other books and spend two hours cross-referencing my options. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I just think using the WtA framework for shamans makes so much more sense because the DNA for it is already burnt into the system.</span></span><br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T17:36:20-07:00","id":1521299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1521189-w20-mini-splat-witches-and-witchers?p=1521252#post1521252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">So, after all that, can I create a working mortal shaman character for WtA with the current rules under S20? Yes, if I use a dozen other books and spend two hours cross-referencing my options. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I just think using the WtA framework for shamans makes so much more sense because the DNA for it is already burnt into the system.</span></span>\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'd be interested in hearing how you would build the same concept using just the W20 corebook, because it sounds like you'll still be doing a lot of customization anyway. But it's your game so if this works out better for you, more power.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T14:53:30-07:00","id":1521350,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Oh, that\u2019s fair! Good idea actually, that should help with finding kinks in the concept.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I will allow myself to reskin stuff to fit the plant theme, that should be fine.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">So, same target list as before. Also skipping over the trivial stuff again.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Totem:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Fireweed isn\u2019t in the core book. We reskin Bear to the plant Spirit Ivy as new Totem (+1 Sta instead of +1 Str).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Interaction with Spirits:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Is an innate ability.</span></span><br /> We will add <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Rite of Summoning (2)</span></span>\u200b<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Spirit Companion:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Covered by the Numina.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Fun with plants:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Rite of Growth (1)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Gift: Create Element (Plants) (1)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Numen \u2013 Vine Spirit (Wyld / Glory)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Charm: Materialize</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Charm: Razor Vines (Blast reskin)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Charm: Entangle (Freeze reskin. Instead of damage, perform a grappling action).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Poison:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Not much here for that. We could cover this with an Ability, but let\u2019s be a little creative and use Rite of Binding (1) to allow the creation of special poisons as Talens.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Rites:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Already covered.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Additional general utility:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Gift: Persuasion (1)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Gift: Breath of the Wyld (1)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Numen \u2013 Mold Spirit (Wyld / Wisdom)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Charm: Cleanse the Blight</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Charm: Realm Sense</span></span><br /> <br /> Sheet mock-up in spoiler tag:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img width=\"657\" height=\"814\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/CrvIiqL.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/CrvIiqL.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/CrvIiqL.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-----</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Things learned: The selection of Charms, Totems, and Renown Types is rather slim with the core book alone. CB20 helps with the latter and expands the Gift lists. For Charms and Totems you have to get more creative than I thought \u2013 there is surprisingly little plant related stuff. Overall it felt less painful to create, but that may be from my practice of using those as NPCs.<br /> <br /> Also, let me emphasize again I'm not dead set on this. Getting reactions here is a good litmus test, and it seems so far people are content with RAW shamans.</span></span><br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T18:39:56-07:00","id":1521360,"title":"","content":"It seems to me that if your solution in W20 is simply to reskin things so they fit, then you eliminate 80% or more of your complaint that you cannot use Sorcerer because you'd need a dozen other sourcebooks and hours of cross referencing. <br /> <br /> If you apply the same principle, you just need Sorcerer (though you prefer Sorcerer 1e over 20 as do I) and reskin Totems, Spirits, and Charms as necessary. If your fun with plants simply becomes customizing your own plant spirits (but calling them Numen) in W20, then you can do the same with Sorcerer contacting specific Plant Spirits that are identical to your previous Numen. Then roleplay actual chiminage.<br /> <br /> So to me it seems like your own issues are 1) your W20 way makes a more powerful character and you prefer that, and 2) you only need one book instead of two. If those two things are that important to you and works for your players, that's fine. But to me it seems like Sorcerer is still the best way to go, but that is probably because I use it heavily in all my games. I think it's an essential sourcebook (I use the first version exclusively combined with some photocopied pages of Hunters Hunted, The Quick &amp; the Dead, and Ascensions Right Hand) for whenever I want an ordinary human who has special knowledge or power. So I don't find it an imposition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T21:33:50-07:00","id":1521362,"title":"","content":"I seem to recall that the Mage book The Spirit Ways had rules for non-Awakened &quot;shaman&quot;/spiritualist/animist characters. I think they were reprinted/refined in the revised Dreamspeakers book. (John Snead, who IIRC is/was a practicing animist, wrote them.)<br /> <br /> Just personally, I've always felt that the best way to do Spirit-Touched humans in Werewolf was to give them Gnosis, a personal Totem, and access to Gifts and Rites that are suitable for their culture/style.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T01:44:53-07:00","id":1521366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1521189-w20-mini-splat-witches-and-witchers?p=1521360#post1521360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to me that if your solution in W20 is simply to reskin things so they fit, then you eliminate 80% or more of your complaint that you cannot use Sorcerer because you'd need a dozen other sourcebooks and hours of cross referencing.<br /> <br /> If you apply the same principle, you just need Sorcerer (though you prefer Sorcerer 1e over 20 as do I) and reskin Totems, Spirits, and Charms as necessary. If your fun with plants simply becomes customizing your own plant spirits (but calling them Numen) in W20, then you can do the same with Sorcerer contacting specific Plant Spirits that are identical to your previous Numen. Then roleplay actual chiminage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I would argue the 80% quota but your point stands. The reason Sorcerer 1e rules are easier to use is because they are less restrictive than S20, but as you said, I would still need to perform the reskinning for the Charms, Spirits, and Totems. I first came up with the idea while creating shaman NPCs when I noticed that I could skip the 'Sorcerer rules layer' of a build, because ultimately the powers the shaman uses are those of the Spirits. That differs from other sorcery where the effects are direct results of the Paths. Narratively, there is no difference - I would still want to roleplay Chiminage, the shaman's Focus, and so on. It just cuts down on a mechanical layer.<br /> By the way, is the idea of making Chiminage a trackable pool stat uncomfortable? I thought it would be a help for players to keep track of things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1521189-w20-mini-splat-witches-and-witchers?p=1521360#post1521360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So to me it seems like your own issues are 1) your W20 way makes a more powerful character and you prefer that, and 2) you only need one book instead of two. If those two things are that important to you and works for your players, that's fine. But to me it seems like Sorcerer is still the best way to go, but that is probably because I use it heavily in all my games. I think it's an essential sourcebook (I use the first version exclusively combined with some photocopied pages of Hunters Hunted, The Quick &amp; the Dead, and Ascensions Right Hand) for whenever I want an ordinary human who has special knowledge or power. So I don't find it an imposition.</div> </div> </div> </div>For 1), somewhat: if your goal is to include a shaman in a mixed WtA campaign, they are still significantly weaker than a full shapechanger. The boost from chargen in getting a Totem and companion Spirits should even out a little with progression.<br /> <br /> Regarding 2), I think it's obvious that I don't shy away from using other material. The comment of the advantage of having a ruleset that is contained to one system mostly applies to new players.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1521189-w20-mini-splat-witches-and-witchers?p=1521362#post1521362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to recall that the Mage book The Spirit Ways had rules for non-Awakened &quot;shaman&quot;/spiritualist/animist characters. I think they were reprinted/refined in the revised Dreamspeakers book. (John Snead, who IIRC is/was a practicing animist, wrote them.)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Spirit Ways is probably one of my all-time favorite WOD books. The Static Shaman in the Dreamspeakers book uses Numina that roughly map to Summoning/Binding/Warding, Ephemera, Enchanting and uniquely Gauntlet Manipulation, although it is a lot more specific in that it uses Essence levels to cap the power of contacted Spirits. Spiritual Awareness is handled with a 4 point Merit and Totem is that of Mage Revised. In that way it is pretty similar to Sorcerer 1e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1521189-w20-mini-splat-witches-and-witchers?p=1521362#post1521362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just personally, I've always felt that the best way to do Spirit-Touched humans in Werewolf was to give them Gnosis, a personal Totem, and access to Gifts and Rites that are suitable for their culture/style.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bDo you cap Gifts/Gnosis as per Kinfolk rules? I found those to be extremely limiting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T15:47:36-07:00","id":1521412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1521189-w20-mini-splat-witches-and-witchers?p=1521366#post1521366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bDo you cap Gifts/Gnosis as per Kinfolk rules? </div> </div> </div> </div>No. IIRC, we went with them automatically starting with Gnosis 1 (as that was what made them Spirit-Touched) and requiring 10 bonus points to get a second dot. I can't recall if it was 2 Gifts and 2 Rites to start off with, or was 3 Gifts and a Rites background. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T13:41:27-07:00","id":1521775,"title":"","content":"Before I shelve this idea, a general question: Do you think skipping the power to invoke spirits (Numina like Ephemera, Summoning, or those in the Dreamspeakers book) would be more or less easy to grasp for new players? I can see arguments for both but my familiarity with the system could blindside me somewhat.<br /> <br /> On one hand having 'something' that represents a character's ability of reach in the Spirit world might help to gauge progress, on the other, directly bargaining with Spirits seems the more natural option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}